# Git branching (RTDMS)

Trunk-based development with **short-lived, zone-scoped** branches. Do not use long-lived
`develop`/`release` branches or commit subsystem work straight to `main`.

## Before any edit

1. `git status` + `git branch --show-current`
2. If on `main` and the task changes code: create/switch to a zone branch first
3. Touch only paths allowed for that zone (table below)

## Branch names

```
<zone>/<short-topic>
```

| Zone prefix | Allowed paths | Typical owner |
|---|---|---|
| `face/` | `models/face/**` | Youssef |
| `physio/` | `models/physiology/**` | Ziad |
| `phone/` | `models/phone/**` | TBD |
| `fusion/` | `fusion/**` | Joint |
| `docs/` | shared status only: root `README.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `Agent Guide.md`, `Home.md`, `models/README.md`, `Subsystems/Models Index.md`, `Subsystems/*` narrative | Anyone |
| `meta/` | `.cursor/rules/**`, `.github/**`, repo tooling | Anyone |

Examples: `face/perclos-window`, `physio/ble-reconnect`, `phone/statefarm-train`, `docs/models-status`.

Also always apply `.cursor/rules/pi-performance-pipeline.mdc` — Pi concurrent performance beats laptop DX.

## Hard rules for agents

- **One zone per branch / PR.** Never mix `models/face/` and `models/physiology/` in the same change.
- **No direct commits to `main`** for model code. Branch → commit → PR (or ask the user to PR).
- **Shared-doc bumps are a separate `docs/` PR** after the code PR merges — not bundled with large code diffs.
- **Sync before finishing:** `git fetch origin && git rebase origin/main` (or merge) on your zone branch so it is not stale.
- **New cross-model contracts** (schemas, sockets): write a short note under `Subsystems/` on a `docs/` branch and get agreement before both sides implement.
- Prefer **small, mergeable slices** over multi-day branches. Incomplete features stay behind flags / unused entrypoints, not on a divergent branch.

## Conflict avoidance checklist

```
❌ edit face + physiology in one PR
❌ commit WIP model code on main
❌ put phone weights under models/face/
❌ invent a fusion JSON shape only on one side

✅ face/<topic> touching only models/face/
✅ physio/<topic> touching only models/physiology/
✅ docs/<topic> for one-line status table updates
```

Full ownership narrative: `models/README.md` → Ownership. Vault: `Subsystems/Models Index.md`.
